“Moved to BLOCKED” — what exactly happens?
===================================================
When a thread calls wait() inside synchronized(buffer):
-------------------------------------------------------
* It releases the monitor lock on buffer
* It transitions to the state WAITING
* It is placed into the object’s Wait Set (conceptually)

Then someone calls notifyAll() (also inside synchronized(buffer))
---------------------------------------------------------------
Important: notifyAll() does not let those threads run immediately, because the notifier still holds the monitor.
So the JVM does this:
* Every thread in the Wait Set is unparked and moved to the Entry Set (conceptually)
* Those threads now need to re-acquire the monitor to continue. Not in a FIFO manner (unfair lock)
* While they are trying to enter synchronized(buffer), their Java thread state shows as BLOCKED (blocked on monitor entry)

So:
* WAITING = “parked, waiting to be notified on this monitor”
* BLOCKED = “awake, but can’t proceed because someone else holds the monitor”

Initial state
===================
1. P1, C1, C2 created but none have entered synchronized(buffer) yet.
======================================================================
 +--------------------------------------------------+
 |                Monitor : buffer                  |
 +--------------------------------------------------+
 | Owner      : NONE                                |
 |                                                  |
 | Entry Set  : [                                  ]| <= not FIFO, BLOCKED
 |                                                  |
 | Wait Set   : [                                  ]| <= WAITING as seen in jstack
 +--------------------------------------------------+

 Threads:
 P1 : NEW / RUNNABLE (not in synchronized)
 C1 : NEW / RUNNABLE (not in synchronized)
 C2 : NEW / RUNNABLE (not in synchronized)


2. C1 enters consume() and reaches wait() (buffer empty, not closed)
=====================================================================

+--------------------------------------------------+
|                Monitor : buffer                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
| Owner      : NONE                                |
|                                                  |
| Entry Set  : [                                  ]|
|                                                  |
| Wait Set   : [ C1                               ]|
+--------------------------------------------------+

Threads:
P1 : RUNNABLE (outside synchronized)
C1 : WAITING  (Object.wait on buffer)
C2 : RUNNABLE (outside synchronized)

3. C2 enters consume() and also reaches wait()
============================================

   +--------------------------------------------------+
   |                Monitor : buffer                  |
   +--------------------------------------------------+
   | Owner      : NONE                                |
   |                                                  |
   | Entry Set  : [                                  ]|
   |                                                  |
   | Wait Set   : [ C1, C2                           ]|
   +--------------------------------------------------+

   Threads:
   P1 : RUNNABLE (outside synchronized)
   C1 : WAITING  (Object.wait on buffer)
   C2 : WAITING  (Object.wait on buffer)

!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! IMPORTANT !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
4. Main thread calls close() and uses notify() (broken case).
===================================================================
After notify() runs, but before close() exits (main still owns the monitor).

+--------------------------------------------------+
|                Monitor : buffer                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
| Owner      : MAIN                                |
|                                                  |
| Entry Set  : [                                ]| <= Note C1 was Notified and is placed under Entry Set because close()
|                                                  |    has still not existed
| Wait Set   : [                                ]|
+--------------------------------------------------+

Threads:
P1   : RUNNABLE (outside synchronized)
C1   : BLOCKED  (woken, trying to re-enter monitor)
C2   : WAITING  (still in wait set)
MAIN : RUNNABLE (inside synchronized close)

5. MAIN exits close() and releases the monitor.
======================================================
   C1 acquires it, re-checks conditions, sees closed && empty, returns null, exits.
   C2 is still stuck waiting forever.

   +--------------------------------------------------+
   |                Monitor : buffer                  |
   +--------------------------------------------------+
   | Owner      : NONE                                |
   |                                                  |
   | Entry Set  : [                                  ]|
   |                                                  |
   | Wait Set   : [ C2                               ]|
   +--------------------------------------------------+

   Threads:
   P1   : RUNNABLE / TERMINATED (not relevant here)
   C1   : TERMINATED
   C2   : WAITING  (Object.wait on buffer)
   MAIN : WAITING  (Thread.join on C2)   // if main joined C2


   6. MAIN calls close() and uses notifyAll()
   =========================================================
   After notifyAll() runs, but before close() exits (MAIN still owns the monitor).

   +--------------------------------------------------+
   |                Monitor : buffer                  |
   +--------------------------------------------------+
   | Owner      : MAIN                                |
   |                                                  |
   | Entry Set  : [ C1, C2                           ]| <= IMPORTANT: both C1 & C2 goes in entry set
   |                                                  |
   | Wait Set   : [                                  ]|
   +--------------------------------------------------+

   Threads:
   P1   : RUNNABLE (outside synchronized)
   C1   : BLOCKED  (woken, trying to re-enter monitor)
   C2   : BLOCKED  (woken, trying to re-enter monitor)
   MAIN : RUNNABLE (inside synchronized close)


  7. MAIN exits close() and releases the monitor.
  =================================================
      C1 acquires monitor, sees closed && empty, exits.
      Then C2 acquires monitor, sees closed && empty, exits.

      +--------------------------------------------------+
      |                Monitor : buffer                  |
      +--------------------------------------------------+
      | Owner      : NONE                                |
      |                                                  |
      | Entry Set  : [                                  ]|
      |                                                  |
      | Wait Set   : [                                  ]|
      +--------------------------------------------------+

      Threads:
      P1   : RUNNABLE / TERMINATED (not relevant here)
      C1   : TERMINATED
      C2   : TERMINATED
      MAIN : RUNNABLE (continues; joins return)